# Example: Defined Terms and Article Semantics

# Define terms with explanations (dash syntax)
liability_cap - the highest amount the liability settlement can go
termination_notice - the number of days required before contract termination
Indemnification Clause - the contract section describing protection from claims

# Load the document
Load document

# Article usage examples:

# "a/an" - introducing a new term (existential quantifier)
Document must contain a Liability Clause
Document must contain an Indemnification Clause

# "the" - referencing a specific/previously mentioned term (definite)
the Document must contain the Termination Clause

# "All" - universal quantifier (every document in scope)
All Documents must contain a Confidentiality Clause

# Extract using defined terms
# The parser will expand liability_cap to its definition for better matching
Find a liability_cap and save as liability_cap
Find a termination_notice and save as termination_notice

# Validate
the liability_cap must be at least 1000000
The termination_notice must be at least 30 days
